<title>USA: Movie Gallery Inc Q4.</title>
<headline>Movie Gallery Inc Q4.</headline>
<dateline>DOTHAN, Ala. 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>				    Q4 Ended	    Year Ended</p>
<p>			     Jan. 5,   Dec. 31,  Jan. 5,   Dec. 31,</p>
<p>				  1997	 1995     1997	1995</p>
<p> Revenues		  $ 69,862  $ 50,064 $254,395   $149,201</p>
<p> Net income (1)	    3,695     3,934    1,606(2) $ 13,437</p>
<p> Net income per share (1) 0.28	0.30     0.12(2) $   1.11</p>
<p>Weighted average shares</p>
<p>   outstanding	     13,423    13,032   13,368     12,153</p>
<p>NOTE: Had the company's new amortization policy for videocassette rental inventory, adopted in the second quarter of 1996, been in effect prior to 1995, net income per share would have grown for the quarter to $0.28 from $0.20 for Q4 1995.</p>
<p>(1) Pro forma adjustments for income taxes have been made as if Home Vision Entertainment Inc and Hollywood Video Inc (1996 acquisitions accounted for as poolings of interests) had been C Corporations instead of S Corporations for the entirety of the periods presented.</p>
<p>(2) Includes a nonrecurring after-tax charge of $4,786, or $0.36 per share, related to a change in amortization policy for videocassette rental inventory and a nonrecurring after-tax charge of $6,470, or $0.48 per share, for store closures, corporate restructuring and merger-related expenses.</p>
</text>
